{"kind":"artifact","text":"Temporal merge staleness at cmd/gs on exact head 8ecd0fe34f11108d87f468163b605a82bfef7bb7, implementing the decision ratified as eae77d2c.\n\nvalidateMerge now asks whether the world had already moved when the verdict was signed, rather than whether anything under it has been retired since. A basis retired before the signing still refuses, which is the strict reading the old gate protected and which is kept. A basis retired afterwards does not, because the commit is immutable and the diff the reviewer read is the diff that lands.\n\nWithdrawal stays outside the clock for what the verdict itself names — its promise and its artifact — because taking either back repudiates the verdict whenever it happens. What an artifact rests on is deliberately excluded: a merge artifact rests on the predecessor its own merge retires, so applying the withdrawal rule there would refuse every succession and reinstate the defect.\n\nNo fold change and no profile bump. Acts carry no sequence, but every act has one decision and decisions are numbered, so retirements are dated by joining them. liveArtifact and liveStatement are removed, having become unreachable.\n\nVerified by mutation: ignoring the signing time fails the after-verdict case while leaving the before-verdict refusal passing; dropping the withdrawal rule fails the repudiation case. Gates at this head: vet, build, full go test ./... with no failures, go test -race on cmd/gs, uncached citation gate, diff-check clean, worktree clean, pushed and matching.\n\nIt rests on the ratified decision, which is what AGENTS.md asks of self-initiated work.","body":{"commit":"8ecd0fe34f11108d87f468163b605a82bfef7bb7","path":"cmd/gs"}}